P3 core prerequisites reused: A1 theme/tokens (TeslaTokens/Spacing/ChartPalette), shared component
  library (ui/charts/datadisplay/feedback/forms/motion), S7/S8 data layer (VehiclesRepository/Store,
  AnalyticsRepository/Store, SettingsRepository/Store), S5 unit conversion (convertDistanceFromSI,
  UnitPreferences), S10 i18n catalog (res/values*), S11 diagnostics (Logger via LocalDataContainer).

Surface files (allowed): apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/CostBreakdownWidget/
 - CostBreakdownModel.kt            (registration, size, prefs, raw-SI JSON decode, projection,
                                     currency/number formatting via ChartFormat, MI_TO_KM cost-per-dist)
 - CostBreakdownSource.kt           (vehicles()+costBreakdown()+settings() seam + Repository & Store adapters)
 - CostBreakdownWidgetViewModel.kt  (BaseFeedViewModel; resolves vehicleId/first vehicle -> /analytics/tco
                                     UiState<JsonElement>; settings -> displayPrefs; refresh; view.opened)
 - CostBreakdownWidget.kt           (stateful + stateless Content; loading/error/empty/compact/standard;
                                     Canvas donut ring; ranked list; 3 StatCards; freshness chip + refresh)
Tests: src/test/.../costbreakdown/{CostBreakdownProjectionTest(15), CostBreakdownWidgetViewModelTest(12)};
       src/androidTest/.../costbreakdown/CostBreakdownWidgetUiTest(7).

Documented deviations (Honesty Covenant #9 — no silent drift):
 1. Gradle module is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts: projectDir=app); the prompt gate's ':app:' does not
    exist in this build. The gate below uses ':android:' (the same skew every sibling P3/A* log documents).
 2. Production files live in the mandated dir com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/CostBreakdownWidget/ but
    declare package io.teslasync.android.dashboard.widgets.costbreakdown — a valid Kotlin package cannot
    contain a hyphen or a PascalCase segment, so detekt InvalidPackageDeclaration + MatchingDeclarationName
    are @file-suppressed with justification (mirrors the ChargeStatusWidget/AutomationHistoryWidget siblings
    at the identical path).
 3. Tests live in the standard src/test + src/androidTest source sets, scoped to this surface. The offline
    gate runs JVM unit tests; the Compose UI/a11y tests are instrumented (connectedAndroidTest, device-only)
    — authored + compile-mirrored on the proven ChargeStatusWidgetUiTest pattern.
 4. Host wiring (grid placement / choosing vehicleId) is outside allowed files; the widget binds the shared
    S7/S8 feeds via an injected CostBreakdownSource (Vehicles + Analytics + Settings adapters, host-ready)
    and derives display prefs (distance unit + currency symbol + precision) from the live /settings feed
    (web useUnits/useFormatting). The cost feed is raw SI JSON (/analytics/tco) decoded in CostBreakdownModel.
 5. PRE-EXISTING, UNRELATED repo breakage — NOT introduced by this change. `git status --short` shows ONLY
    the new costbreakdown + CostBreakdownWidget dirs as untracked additions; no tracked file is modified in
    the committed change set. Three sibling defects (all OUTSIDE this artifact's allowed files) sit at this
    worktree's HEAD:
      (a) CONFLICTING top-level fun resolveVehicleId(Long?, List<Vehicle>?) in package
          io.teslasync.android.dashboardwidgets — ChargeHistoryWidgetModel.kt:86 (-> Long) vs
          BatteryDegradationTrendWidgetViewModel.kt:104 (-> Long?). Two identical-signature top-level
          declarations in one package => "Conflicting overloads" => :android:compileReleaseKotlin FAILS
          module-wide on a clean checkout. Both files belong to OTHER surfaces (ChargeHistory,
          BatteryDegradationTrend). This conflict did NOT exist when sibling 0021/ChargeStatusWidget ran
          (its log records assembleRelease=0); it appeared after those two surfaces were both merged.
      (b) BatteryCellsWidgetTest.kt — 5 unit tests fail (pre-existing; the 0021 log already documents the
          root cause: its private viewModel() helper omits backgroundScope so stateIn never advances).
      (c) BatteryCellsWidgetUiTest.kt:7 — unresolved reference 'assertExists' (a compile error in the
          shared androidTest source set).
    Isolation method (mirrors the 0021 predecessor's "move the broken sibling aside, compile, restore"):
    to compile the module and run THIS artifact's scoped gate, defect (a) was temporarily resolved by
    renaming the BatteryDegradationTrend helper resolveVehicleId -> resolveDegradationVehicleId (its decl +
    1 call + its own 4 test calls), the gate was run, then the rename was REVERTED via `git checkout`. The
    committed change set therefore contains ONLY this artifact's files (git status re-confirmed post-revert).
    Consequence on the SHARED tasks: clean-HEAD :android:assembleRelease is blocked by (a); repo-wide
    :android:testReleaseUnitTest is blocked by (a) then (b); :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin is
    blocked by (c). This artifact's SCOPED gate (with (a) temporarily isolated) is all green and introduces
    0 new failures.

